        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "711bf03c-b36a-56ee-b547-085deebce451",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: KSPN-FM, Talking Heads\n- People: David Byrne, Stephen Thomas Erlewine\n- Topics: AAA format, new wave music\n\nFacts:\n- David Byrne was born on 14 May 1952 and is a Scottish-born American musician.\n- Talking Heads were an American rock band formed in 1975 in New York City and active until 1991.\n- David Byrne was the founding member, principal songwriter, lead singer, and guitarist of Talking Heads during the band's 1975 to 1991 run.\n- Talking Heads helped pioneer new wave music by combining punk, art rock, funk, and world music with avant-garde sensibilities and an anxious, clean-cut image.\n- Critic Stephen Thomas Erlewine described Talking Heads as one of the most critically acclaimed bands of the 1980s.\n- KSPN-FM features the AAA format, mixing classic rock artists including Tom Petty, Van Morrison, and Talking Heads with newer musicians such as Ben Harper, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, and Widespread Panic.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "647775d3-3390-583b-a27d-41cf6629c67b",
        "text": "Page: KSPN-FM. Sentence: KSPN features the AAA format, which combines the classic rock hits from Tom Petty, Van Morrison and Talking Heads with today’s newer musicians like Ben Harper, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada and Widespread Panic.\nPage: Talking Heads. Sentence: Talking Heads were an American rock band formed in 1975 in New York City and active until 1991.\nPage: Talking Heads. Sentence: Described by critic Stephen Thomas Erlewine as \"one of the most critically acclaimed bands of the '80s,\" the group helped to pioneer new wave music by integrating elements of punk, art rock, funk, and world music with avant-garde sensibilities and an anxious, clean-cut image.\nPage: David Byrne. Sentence: David Byrne ( ; born 14 May 1952) is a Scottish-born American musician who was the founding member, principal songwriter, and lead singer and guitarist of the American new wave band Talking Heads, active between 1975 and 1991.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
